<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Stocks drift in listless trade.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Stocks drift in listless trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks drifted in listless after-hours trading following the losses suffered during normal trading hours, dealers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a trade here and there but I don't see anything active,&quot; said one of them.</p>
<p>Cisco Systems Inc was one of the few stocks that was trading but volume was low, she said.</p>
<p>The company's stock was up to 59-1/4 in after hours trading against a Nasdaq close of 58-3/4.  </p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Wednesday that session one had a volume of 24,300 shares against the previous day's 7,700. Session two had 2.99 million compared to 2.4 million, it said.</p>
